/-!
# BCG01's index-shifted binding at BBR03's counterexample sequence (lane BDRY-IDX4)

Consumer (non-vacuity) of `bcg01_boundary_support_lists_BCG1_IDX4`: the accepted
`bcg01_boundary_support_lists_BCG1` takes a sequence at `δ_n` for ALL `n`, an EMPTY hypothesis
(`isEmpty_boundarySequence_ratio_IDX`); the restated binding takes the sequence at `δ_{n+1}`, the
TYPE produced by BBR03's framework `exists_boundary_counterexample_sequence_of_no_threshold`
(`StaticCounterexamples.lean`, B:10624–10625). `bcg01_boundary_support_lists_bbr03_IDX4` applies
it there without an adapter: for every certificate `Good` without a nonempty-boundary threshold,
BBR03's counterexample sequence (no member satisfies `Good`) carries BCG01's whole tail.
-/

